Gonna be a fun one, @romainhuet @embirico.

@LargeLangMammal shared an AI Engineer World's Fair 2026 schedule presented as a simple, searchable table. You can click values to filter and press esc to clear. The table is hosted on Cloudflare, with search by @turbopuffer and the table layout by #aiewf and @aiDotEngineer.

The schedule is available on aie.lite.cat, and the table implementation is based on a single-page, URL-addressable list table from GitHub at deshitifai/tabelle.

Few things you might have missed in last week's announcement. The update includes an easier way to review pull requests, the ability to edit code directly in Codex, and enhancements to Computer Use.

The author appreciates the ability to quickly edit code in the diff for small additions or debugging without using many tokens.

@romainhuet: "Here’s what’s new in Codex for developers! Thanks for helping us make it better. See Codex handle hard tasks with GPT‑5.6, work in parallel, use the computer, edit code inline, and review PRs. Watch the end: something that isn’t out yet makes a cameo."

